## Architecture: CQRS

```
HTTP Request → Router → Controller → CommandBus/QueryBus → Handler → Repository
```

- **Commands** mutate state (Create, Update, Delete)
- **Queries** read state (GetById, List)
- Never call the repository directly from the controller — always go through the bus.

## Adding a new module

1. Create `src/features/<moduleName>/` with the following structure:
```
<moduleName>/
├── <moduleName>.routes.ts            ← composition root (wire everything here)
├── commands/
│   ├── create-<moduleName>.command.ts
│   ├── create-<moduleName>.handler.ts
│   ├── update-<moduleName>.command.ts
│   ├── update-<moduleName>.handler.ts
│   └── delete-<moduleName>.handler.ts
├── queries/
│   ├── get-<moduleName>.query.ts
│   ├── get-<moduleName>.handler.ts
│   ├── list-<moduleName>s.query.ts
│   └── list-<moduleName>s.handler.ts
├── domain/
│   ├── <moduleName>.entity.ts
│   ├── <moduleName>.repository.interface.ts
│   └── <moduleName>.events.ts
├── infrastructure/
│   ├── bus.ts                         ← already shared, reuse the bus interfaces
│   ├── <moduleName>.controller.ts
│   └── <moduleName>.repository.ts
└── dto/
    ├── create-<moduleName>.dto.ts
    └── <moduleName>.response.ts
```

2. Register the router in `src/app.ts`:
```ts
import { {{camelCase moduleName}}Router } from './features/<moduleName>/<moduleName>.routes';
// ...
app.use({{camelCase moduleName}}Router.routes());
app.use({{camelCase moduleName}}Router.allowedMethods());
```

## Koa specifics

- Use `ctx.body` to set response, `ctx.status` for HTTP status
- Access request body via `ctx.request.body` (parsed by koa-bodyparser)
- Route params via `ctx.params.id`
- Query strings via `ctx.query.limit`
- Throw `AppError` / `NotFoundError` from `src/errors/app-error` — the error handler middleware catches them
- No `res.send()`, no `next()` callbacks — pure async/await
